---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import { releaseSource } from "../../data/navigation";
const buildRequest = [
  "python3 - <<'PY' > request.json",
  "import json, uuid",
  "from pathlib import Path",
  "",
  "request = {",
  '    "schema_version": 3,',
  '    "execution_mode": "native",',
  '    "request_id": str(uuid.uuid4()),',
  '    "project_dir": str(Path.cwd().resolve()),',
  '    "cli": "codex",',
  '    "model_selection": {"kind": "explicit", "id": "gpt-6.1-sol"},',
  '    "instructions": "Rewrite the supplied question for clarity. Return only the revision.",',
  '    "input": "how exactly is cache invalidation handled here?",',
  '    "timeout_seconds": 120,',
  "}",
  "print(json.dumps(request, ensure_ascii=False))",
  "PY",
].join("\n");
---

<Docs
  title="Generation requests & results"
  description="Give one installed agent a bounded text task. Capture the inputs before launch and validate the terminal result before using its output."
  toc={[
    ["first", "Send a request"],
    ["schema", "Choose a schema"],
    ["result", "Read the terminal result"],
    ["exit", "Handle failure"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="first">Send a request</h2>
  <p>
    Start in a trusted project with an admitted, signed-in Codex CLI. Approve
    the intended folder once. The sample writes <code>request.json</code> and{" "}
    <code>result.json</code> in the current folder, so use a disposable project
    when trying it. Generation runs with the native agent’s headless
    permissions, which may allow file edits and integrations.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · approve the current project"
    code={'clink allow "$(pwd -P)" --cli codex'}
  />
  <Code label="Terminal · create request.json" code={buildRequest} />
  <Code
    label="Terminal · run one generation attempt"
    code={
      'clink generate --request-json - < request.json > result.json\nresult_code=$?\nprintf "Clink exit code: %s\\n" "$result_code"\ncat result.json'
    }
  />
  <h2 id="schema">Choose a schema</h2>
  <p>
    Use native <strong>schema 3</strong> for typed selection. Codex and Claude
    Code require <code>{'{"kind":"explicit","id":"…"}'}</code> with a native
    model ID. Claude requires a concrete full model name. Grok uses{" "}
    <code>{'{"kind":"native_default"}'}</code>. Antigravity accepts that
    selection shape and currently refuses generation. The older native{" "}
    <strong>schema 2</strong> uses an explicit top-level <code>model</code> for
    Codex or Claude. Schema 1’s no-tools profile is currently refused.
  </p>
  <p>
    Supply a canonical, existing absolute <code>project_dir</code>,{" "}
    <code>execution_mode: "native"</code>, a fresh UUID and the exact
    instruction and input strings. A request can contain up to 64 KiB of
    instructions and 256 KiB of input, within a 1 MiB raw request limit. Close
    stdin within ten seconds. <code>timeout_seconds</code> defaults to 120 and
    accepts 1–1,800 seconds, including intake and queueing.
  </p>
  <h2 id="result">Read the terminal result</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>
      <code>status</code>, <code>output</code>, <code>truncated</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Use the text only after exit 0, a completed status, and a nonblank,
      untruncated result. Other statuses include failed, incomplete, timed_out
      and cancelled.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>request_id</code> and three SHA-256 fields
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Match the UUID and the request, instruction and input hashes to your
      submitted values. The effective request hash excludes the UUID and
      represents timeout in milliseconds. The{" "}
      <a href="/extensions/ask-repo/">ask_repo example</a> performs these
      checks.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>execution</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Inspect the selected CLI, model selection and project. The CLI-reported
      actual model may be null. Native permissions can produce side effects
      before failure. Completion confirms final-response transport.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>error</code>, <code>warnings</code>, <code>duration_ms</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Use the public error code and the duration for diagnostics. Keep private
      prompts and raw sessions out of logs.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <h2 id="exit">Handle failure</h2>
  <div
    class="table-scroll"
    role="region"
    aria-label="Generation exit codes"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Exit</th>
          <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {[
          [0, "Completed"],
          [
            1,
            "Execution, admission, authentication, parser or transport failure",
          ],
          [2, "Invalid invocation, input or request limit"],
          [3, "Incomplete result"],
          [124, "Deadline exceeded"],
          [130, "Cancelled"],
        ].map(([code, meaning]) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{code}</th>
            <td>{meaning}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Some early invocation errors only produce command-line diagnostics. Inspect
    the exit status even if stdout is empty. Clink makes at most one top-level
    attempt per accepted request. Check possible effects before submitting
    again. For cross-language encoding and result fields, see the{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docs/generation-native-protocol.md"}>schema 2</a>{" "}
    and{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docs/generation-native-families.md"}>schema 3</a>{" "}
    contracts.
  </p>
</Docs>
